Applies a function to every item of a list. The input is the pair [f xs]: f is a function of one argument, and the output is the list of its results. Each result is computed when its item is reached.
---

---
(fn p
  (letrec m (fn l (if (? l) ~ [((head p) (head l)) (m (tail l))]))
    (m (tail p))))
---
[(fn x (+ x 1)) [1 2 3 ~]] => [2 3 4 ~] fuel 100000
[(fn x x) ~] => ~ fuel 100000
[(fn x (* x x)) [3 -4 ~]] => [9 16 ~] fuel 100000
